# Pilot of permuted neighbours on the mini's compare lanes: pre-registration (DRAFT of 2026-11-24, evening, for mmdbbench#164)

Status: DRAFT. Nothing has run on the mini, nothing is queued, nothing is posted. It becomes the pre-registration when I post it on #164 with the lock block of section 12 filled in by `build_prereg.py` (the hashes of the files). From then on every value below changes only by my word, and a change after the first run of a leg makes it a new pilot (the rule of the lane qualification plans of 2026-11-18 to 2026-11-22). This file lives in the notes of the benchmark repo, which has no remote. It replaces the draft of the morning of the same day.

Every number in this file is written by `build_prereg.py` from the output of the scripts named in section 12 (`select_cells.py`, `plan.py`, `cost_legs.py`, `smoke.py`, `smoke_runner.py`), or is a design constant of #164 (5 runs per target and level, 3 solo runs, 3 percent) or of the lane documentation, and the cited ones are checked against the file they come from.

## 0. What changed since the draft of the morning

- My decisions of 2026-11-24 on #164 (comment of 2026-11-23, read again): n=5 means 5 runs per target and neighbour level; the real cells cover the disk I/O and the cache and latency classes; for compute and memory bandwidth the calibration probes `cpu` and `membw` are the targets and the report says so; the non-compute classes get their qualification through a pre-registered plan written first (`QUALIFICATION-PLAN.md`), never by relabelling a job's class.
- When: not January. The mini is idle now and the 26.12.1 small pass starts after the engine release (about 2026-12-02), so the legs that the record admits today run this week, and the 26.12.1 pass can use three lanes if they pass.
- Heat: the mini throttled with three busy compare lanes (humem-ops#480: 91 C, 33 to 48 s of throttle per job on 2026-11-22, and two busy lanes also throttled later that night). So a block has at most two busy lanes, the third lane carries a light neighbour, a thermal gate and a throttle reading belong to every run, and a separate heat run (leg H) measures three busy lanes for 30 minutes before any pass uses three.
- The design follows the record: the order only puts a class on a lane that the mini's record admits (section 8). That is why the legs below are not the full square of the issue; the full square needs the qualification plan first.

## 1. Question

Can the absolute figure of a cell be recovered from runs on compare lanes beside permuted neighbours, within 3 percent of its solo figure, for each resource class (compute, memory bandwidth, disk I/O, cache and latency)? The lane documentation (humem-ops `docs/lanes.md`, "Absolute figures") says a compute-bound cell beside compute neighbours stays close to solo, and that memory-bound and disk-bound cells beside other jobs are biased. Averaging over random neighbours does not remove that bias, so the pilot estimates the neighbour effect and reports the idle-neighbour figure with its interval.

This is a pilot of the method on the small size, where a run takes minutes and a mistake is cheap. It is not a benchmark row, and no figure from it goes on the page or into a paper.

## 2. Targets

Two kinds, as decided on #164.

- Stand-ins for the classes that have no eligible real cell: the calibration probes `cpu` (class compute) and `membw` (class memory bandwidth) of the lane kit, time boxed (60 s each), one figure per run (operations per second, megabytes per second). The report calls their class verdicts PROBE-PASS or PROBE-FAIL and never PASS.
- Real cells for disk I/O and for cache and latency: the four cells of `picks.json`, chosen by `select_cells.py` before any run by the rule written in its docstring (one ArcadeDB arm of a small-size cell of the 26.11.1 landing; a median wall time of at least 60 s; at most 1.5 cores used on average; a memory cap of at most the 12 GiB of a compare lane; jvm before native, embedded before server, shortest first). They are two cells of one family (`l2` interactive graph OLTP at `sf1`) in two durability classes, so a verdict is about that family, not about the class. They are legs L5 and L6 and are not claimable yet (section 9).

The rule was fixed after I had seen the row totals of cpu time, I/O and peak memory per cell, and before any wall time, class or pick was computed. The thresholds were not changed after the pick was printed.

